  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 151 PM EST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nBy Thursday, the area will be between two upper level patterns with \na cutoff low over the northern gulf coast and the wedge firmly \nentrenched into northeast Georgia. Although models have come into \nbetter agreement on the lows positioning into the the northern gulf \ncoast and southwestern GA, models notoriously underestimate how \nstrong the wedge is this far out. On the northeastern side of the \nlow pressure expecting showers to push in from southern Georgia into \ncentral Georgia with 15-35% rain chances through at least Friday. \nPushing into Saturday there is some indication that rain chances \ncould reach into western Georgia but chances remain low at 20-35%. \nThe low pressure system is expected to move out of Georgia by Sunday \ninto Monday next week with only lingering rain chances. Winds will \nremain breezy across central Georgia as this area is between the two \npatterns with sustained winds at 10-15mph and gusts up to 25mph each \nday through the weekend. Increased cloud cover will aid in keeping \novernight temps 10-15 degrees above normal through the weekend with \nupper 40s to mid 50s expected. As for high temperatures they will \nremain just above normal in the mid to upper 60s each day.",
